Package: zugeo
Title: 'GeoArrow' Geometry Columns, Exact or an Error
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Dewey", "Dunnington", role = "cph",
           comment = "geoarrow-c, bundled in src/vendor/geoarrow"),
    person("The Apache Software Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "nanoarrow, bundled in src/vendor/nanoarrow"),
    person("Ulf", "Adams", role = "cph",
           comment = "ryu, bundled in src/vendor/geoarrow/ryu"))
Description: Makes 'GeoArrow' geometry columns first-class R vectors.
    Points, lines and polygons stay in 'Apache Arrow' memory with their
    coordinate reference system and edge type, move between the native,
    well-known binary and well-known text encodings exactly or raise an
    error, and get bounding boxes, spatial sorting and packed spatial
    indexes computed over the coordinate buffers. The bundled 'geoarrow-c'
    library (<https://github.com/geoarrow/geoarrow-c>) needs no system
    library. The format is specified at <https://geoarrow.org/>.
